<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Introduction to Databases</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Calibri, new times roman;
            margin: 20px;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
            color: #333;
        }
        header {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 10px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        section {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .highlight {
            background-color: #eaf2f8;
            padding: 10px;
            border-left: 4px solid #3498db;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        table, th, td {
            border: 1px solid #aaa;
        }
        th, td {
            padding: 8px;
            text-align: left;
        }
        footer {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 30px;
            font-size: 0.9em;
            color: #555;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>📊 INTRODUCTION TO DATABASES</h1>
        <p>Understanding how data is stored, managed, and retrieved</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>What is a Database?</h2>
        <p>A <strong>Database</strong> is an organized collection of data that can be easily accessed, managed, and updated. 
        Databases are used in banking, e-commerce, healthcare, education, and almost every modern industry.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Types of Databases</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Relational Databases (SQL):</b> Store data in tables with rows and columns.</li>
            <li><b>NoSQL Databases:</b> Store data in flexible formats like documents or key-value pairs.</li>
            <li><b>Cloud Databases:</b> Hosted online for scalability and easy access.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Example: Customer Table</h2>
        <div class="highlight">
            <p>Here’s a simple table showing customer data in a relational database:</p>
        </div>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>CustomerID</th>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Email</th>
                <th>Join Date</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>101</td>
                <td>Jane Doe</td>
                <td>jane@example.com</td>
                <td>2023-05-12</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>102</td>
                <td>John Smith</td>
                <td>john@example.com</td>
                <td>2023-06-01</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </section>

    <footer>
        <p>Created as a simple HTML guide to databases 🌐</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
